{
 "schema": 24,
 "id": "boss-bd2-aion",
 "name": "Boss BD-2 (Aion Sapphire)",
 "version": {
  "major": 1,
  "minor": 0
 },
 "description": "Boss BD-2 Blues Driver (1995) as Aion FX's Sapphire (document 1.0.1), the stock circuit with true bypass: an input buffer, two of Boss's discrete op-amps (a JFET pair and a PNP) with diodes clipping between them, a fixed treble cut, Tone, Volume and an op-amp stage that lifts the bass. Aion's Bass knob is drawn at 0, the stock BD-2. Drive is a dual pot (VR1A, VR1B): one knob turns both stages. The JFETs are 2SK209-GR, Aion's (the SMD 2SK184-GR); 2N3906, 2N5088 and RC4558 as Aion's substitutes.",
 "tags": [
  "overdrive"
 ],
 "starter": true,
