 "notes": {
  "part:RPD1": "Aion's RPD: the input pull-down, so the bypass switch doesn't pop.",
  "part:Q1": "Input buffer (source follower), biased at VB by R2.",
  "part:Q2": "Q2 and Q3 are a JFET differential pair; with Q4 they make a discrete op-amp. Q2's gate is the + input, Q3's the − input.",
  "part:VR1B": "Drive, first stage's gang (Aion's GAINB) of the dual 250kA pot: the stage's gain is about 1 + (R8 + VR1B) / R7.",
  "part:VR1A": "Drive, second stage's gang (Aion's GAINA): about 1 + (R19 + VR1A) / R18.",
  "part:C3": "With R7, sets the first stage's gain and its bass cut (no gain at DC, so the stage stays biased at VB).",
  "part:R11": "R11 with C6, and R12, C7, C8 with R13 and R14, shape the signal into the clipping diodes: they pass the highs and trim the bass.",
  "part:D2": "Two diodes in series each way to ground (D2-D5): the signal clips at about ±1.2 V between the stages.",
  "part:C14": "With R22 a fixed treble cut; C13 across R22 lets some highs through.",
  "part:VR2": "Tone: a passive treble cut.",
  "part:IC1B": "Bass boost: Q8 with C19, C20 and R25 is a gyrator (a simulated inductor) in the feedback; the stage lifts the low end. D6 and D7 clip softly between its inputs on loud peaks.",
  "part:VR4": "Bass (Aion's addition): 0 is the stock BD-2 (R24 6k8 alone); fully up is near the Galaxie mod's 33k.",
  "part:Q9": "Output buffer (emitter follower).",
  "part:Q10": "Ripple filter: R32 and C23 smooth Q10's base, its emitter follows as VA. D1 is reverse-polarity protection.",
  "part:IC1A": "Buffers VB, half of VA (R33, R34), the bias for every stage.",
  "net:clip": "After the first stage's clipping diodes, on to the second stage through C9."
 },
